# `bun <file>` and the plain executable fold `true && f`, `f || 1`, `null ?? f`, `1 ? f : 0` to the one operand before the engine sees them: a function or class without a name then stands next to the name that it is given to
# and takes it. (By the language it would not.) The front end gave the name to the operator, which dropped it. What is folded is asked of the one model of what `bun run` knows and leaves out (src/sema/fold).
# The last three stay operators in `bun <file>`: no name. The file is CommonJS so that the shell does not run the source itself: it folds nothing, and by the language none of these takes a name.
# THE RED CONTROL: find_operand_named_in_place_of() answers None: eleven empty names in front.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: "first" "second" "third" "fourth" "fifth" "sixth" "seventh" "eighth" "field" "#hidden" "member" "inner" "" "" ""
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=none
# NONE: "first" "second" "third" "fourth" "fifth" "sixth" "seventh" "eighth" "field" "#hidden" "member" "inner" "" "" ""
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
